From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tseng <tseng.jayj@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] consensus: fix the MeepHash seed schedule and stop priming
 RandomX

MeepCoin block proof-of-work is MeepHash-W v2 at every height, but two
inherited Monero RandomX paths were still live. One could change consensus;
the other did unused work at startup. No consensus value changes.

THE SEED SCHEDULE IS NO LONGER ENVIRONMENT-DEPENDENT

rx_seedheight() picks which block's id seeds MeepHash at height h: the daemon
feeds that id as both the MeepHash epoch key and its delayed-seed input. It
read SEEDHASH_EPOCH_BLOCKS and SEEDHASH_EPOCH_LAG from the environment and let
any power of two up to 2048 and 64 replace the constants. Measured on the
pinned source: SEEDHASH_EPOCH_BLOCKS=1024 put height 1089 on seed 1024 instead
of 0, and SEEDHASH_EPOCH_LAG=32 put heights 2081 and 2112 on seed 2048
instead of 0. Two identical binaries could therefore disagree about the
proof-of-work of a block from the first epoch boundary on. Both reads are
removed; the rule is fixed at compile time:

  seed_height(h) = 0                               when h <= 2048 + 64
                 = (h - 64 - 1) & ~(2048 - 1)      otherwise

rx_seedheights() uses the same constant for the announced next seed. Main
chain, block template, get_miner_data, alternative chain and the template RPC
all call these two functions, unchanged. The block id AT the seed height is
still what MeepHash is given.

NO RANDOMX PRIMING FOR BLOCK PROOF-OF-WORK

Blockchain::init, pop_blocks, switch_to_alternative_blockchain and
handle_block_to_main_chain called rx_set_main_seedhash(), which starts a
background RandomX main-cache (and, with MONERO_RANDOMX_FULL_MEM, dataset)
initialization. Nothing on the block path reads that cache: get_block_longhash
and get_altblock_longhash call meep_slow_hash. Its large-page allocation threw
the caught std::bad_alloc logged at every daemon start. The four calls are
removed; the seed id computed in the reorg and add-block paths is kept for the
miner notification it feeds. The built-in miner's rx_set_miner_thread(), which
marked the thread as a RandomX miner and allocated and initialized the full
RandomX dataset, is removed for the same reason: the miner hashes through
get_block_longhash.

RETAINED, DELIBERATELY

RandomX hashing for RPC payments (src/rpc/rpc_payment.cpp in the daemon,
src/wallet/wallet_rpc_payments.cpp in the wallet) is not block proof-of-work
and is unchanged; without the removed priming it uses RandomX's secondary
light-mode cache for the requested seed. rx_set_main_seedhash(),
rx_set_miner_thread() and external/randomx remain, uncalled or
RPC-payment-only. core::get_block_sync_size() still reads
SEEDHASH_EPOCH_BLOCKS: it clamps how many blocks one sync request may carry
and changes no seed height.

TESTS

  meepcoin-runtime-quarantine-test        79 passed, 0 failed (was 45)
  meepcoin_runtime_quarantine_guards.sh   89 passed, 0 failed (was 81)

The new runtime sections check the boundaries 0, 2112, 2113, 4160 and 4161,
every height 0..8400 against the independently written rule, and re-execute
the test binary as child processes with six adversarial SEEDHASH_EPOCH_*
settings: seed heights, seed block ids and MeepHash outputs must be
byte-identical to the unset baseline. The same test built against the pinned
rx-slow-hash.c fails four of those six (75 passed, 4 failed). The committed v16
daemon-generated block vectors are reproduced through the main-chain
derivation and get_altblock_longhash, with the difficulty-500 target boundary.
The guards assert no caller of rx_set_main_seedhash or rx_set_miner_thread,
rx_slow_hash only in the two RPC-payment files, and the exact set of
seed-height callers.

OUT OF SCOPE, DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED

MeepHash sources and build inputs, genesis values, block vectors, target
comparison, rewards, emission, timestamps, difficulty, hardforks, ports,
address prefixes and wallet formats are byte-identical.

